Suaradee v0.1

Code and model weights: Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE), except lexicon_e.json, which is CC BY-SA 4.0 (see below).

Built on, with thanks:
- Paradee-8M v1.3 by Sahil Mahendrakar (Apache-2.0): the 8M-parameter architecture, the training recipe and the starting
  weights. https://huggingface.co/sahilmahendrakar/Paradee-8M-v1.3
- Kokoro-82M by hexgrad (Apache-2.0): the text encoder whose phoneme features the text side learns to predict, and the
  178-symbol phoneme vocabulary. https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M
- Chatterbox Multilingual by Resemble AI (MIT): generated the synthetic Malay speech the model was trained on.
- misaki (Apache-2.0): English word pronunciations in lexicon_en.json were taken from its US dictionaries.
- Training sentences: Tatoeba (CC BY 2.0 FR), Malay Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0) and sentence templates written for this
  project. The sentences are used only as prompts; no recordings of people were used.

lexicon_e.json (which Malay words use the pepet vowel and which the taling vowel) is derived from:
- WikiPron Malay and Indonesian pronunciation lists, extracted from Wiktionary (CC BY-SA 4.0). This derived file is
  therefore shared under CC BY-SA 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
- g2p-id schwa dictionary (MIT).
- Hand corrections written for this project.
